<!--
  Commander Battle's Khuzait troop classes, merged into Native's mpclassdivisions.xml (MPClassDivisions, MultiplayerGame
  only). Same rules as cb_mpclassdivisions_vlandia.xml:
  - One class per weight of a formation class (role): infantry medium/light, ranged light/heavy, cavalry light/heavy,
    horse archers light/heavy. The weight label comes from the multiplier bands per role (CommanderRoles.WeightBands).
  - The culture's first 7 classes take over its 7 stock class ids in place (_replaceWhileMerging="true"), so they keep the
    stock index (MissionPeer.SelectedTroopIndex) and every class of the culture is ours. Further classes get new cb_ ids
    and are appended. Never put _replaceWhileMerging on a NEW id: with no id match the merger replaces the FIRST class
    of the file instead (MBObjectManager.MergeElements).
  - At most 16 classes per culture (the troop index is 4 bits).
  - multiplier: the class's size weight. A formation fields budget x ceil(100 x multiplier) / the average of its role's
    classes, so it only compares within a role.
  - The only perk list (perk_list="1") is the weapon setups. Index 0 is the class's own loadout; the others swap weapon
    slots with AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn (target Any: commander and troops). No TroopCountOnSpawn: only the weight sets
    the count. game_mode="all": the server's GameType is CommanderBattle, so stock "Captain" perks would never apply.
    AI-led formations get a setup too (MissionMultiplayerCommanderBattle.AssignDefaultClasses), picked by index in the
    plan's order (docs/plans/troop-types.md, "Culture variance pass"), so every role lists its setups in that order.
  - Every weight of a role offers the role's setups in the same order, on its own armour.
  - Khuzait (variance pass): horse-archer doctrine and lancers with tough small shields; the weakest infantry (light and
    medium only, small wicker or round shields, no pikes) and the lightest foot archers. No throwing weapons.
  - Sidearm (Item2) rule: spears and lances keep the culture's sidearm, since they fight poorly up close. Sabres, and
    the swung two-handed glaive, clear it: their main weapon already is one. The glaive clears the shield slot (Item1)
    as well (an AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn without item sets an empty element: AlternativeEquipmentEffect.Deserialize).
  - Horse archers carry no shield: bow (Item0), arrows (Item1) and a sabre (Item2); "bow and glaive" puts the glaive in
    Item2 instead of the sabre.
  - A bad node makes the loader drop every later entry of this file silently; the CommanderBattle log lists the
    classes per culture when a mission opens.
  - Items only from Native's mpitems.xml (the only items multiplayer loads).
-->
